+## ✅ DONE — THEIR PUBLISHED NUMBERS ARE READ (companion v1.9)
+
+**The payload is not the page.** `pick()` walked `initialData`, every metric read null, and the conclusion
+drawn was "they compute client-side, so we must compute too". WRONG — the numbers are in the
+server-rendered MARKUP outside `__NEXT_DATA__`. Verified with NO JavaScript running:
+`Zero Gamma 7646.90 · Call Wall 7900 · Put Wall 7500 · ATM IV 6.2 · P/C 1.36 · Term Slope 1.3`.
+
+`pub` now resolves **payload field -> tree walk -> rendered header**, and **`pubSrc` records which source
+won** for each value.
+
+⚠ **v1.9 SHIPPED THIS BROKEN AND THE TEST PASSED.** An ordered alternation truncated every level to three
+digits — Zero Gamma reached the face as **764 beside a spot of 7674**, under THEIR name, sourced `IF·pub`.
+The test's fixture used `$7,646.90` WITH a comma; the page renders `$7646.90` without one. **A fixture
+invented to suit the parser tests the parser against itself — always take the fixture from the real
+artefact.** Fixed in v1.10, verified against the exact strings their page serves.
+**`levelSane()` is the durable guard**: every price LEVEL must sit within 0.5x–2x of spot or it is refused
+and `pubSrc` records `REJECTED:header=764`. Ratios/IV/slopes are not gated. The gate, not the regex, is
+what makes the NEXT unpredicted parser failure visible. `ifLadder` already preferred `c.pub.zeroGamma`, so FLIP should now render from
+`IF·pub` instead of the computed `FLIP*`/`calc` fallback. **UNVERIFIED LIVE — confirm on Monday.**
+
+⚠ **Their header walls are ALL-EXPIRY; our CR0/PS0 are 0DTE.** Both are "their values", answering
+different questions. `pub.wallsAreAllExpiry` travels with the data. Never substitute one for the other.
+
+### ⛔ THE TAPEREADER'S `ifFetch` MUST STAY OFF — I RECOMMENDED FLIPPING IT ON AND I WAS WRONG
+A cross-origin fetch needs `@grant GM_xmlhttpRequest`. The tapereader runs **`@grant none`, and that is
+LOAD-BEARING**: it keeps the script in PAGE context so its `window.fetch` / `XMLHttpRequest` hooks capture
+Skylit's `gex/levels` feed. Any `@grant` moves it into Tampermonkey's sandbox where `window` is a wrapper
+and the hooks patch the wrapper — **the tape goes dark.** This is stated in the source at the `IF_LS`
+declaration and it is why `IF_CFG` defaults `{on:false}`. The tapereader's `ifFetch`/`ifParse`/`ifLevels`
+are DEAD CODE kept for reference. **The companion holds the grant; anything cross-origin belongs there.**
