+## 🔁 LAST-SESSION MODE (v11.55) — THE PANEL WORKS ON A WEEKEND
+
+When today has no RTH bars, the whole panel replays **the last session in the feed** as if it were the day.
+The face shows a purple `▮ MM/DD REPLAY` chip IN PLACE OF the phase tag. `__gptsDebug.session()` reports
+`{showing, replay, today, rth, recording}`.
+
+**Three guards, and they are the point of the feature — do not weaken them:**
+1. **NEVER during RTH.** An empty today during a live session stays empty. Yesterday must never read as now.
+2. **THE RECORDER WRITES NOTHING** in replay — all five entry points. Replayed bars would poison every
+   base rate in `data/*.json` permanently and undetectably.
+3. **THE FACE SAYS SO.** A mode you cannot see is a mode that lies.
+
+⚠ **`inReplay()` fails TOWARD recording, deliberately**, and every call site uses
+`typeof inReplay==='function' && inReplay()`. A bare global inside those try/catch bodies is the
+swallowed-ReferenceError shape that has bitten this project three times now — and it bit again DURING this
+build (an edit asserted, `SESSION_DAY` was referenced 5x and declared 0x). Had it shipped, the recorder
+would have died silently. A lost session is loud; a dead recorder is not.
