+**purple accelerates · yellow brakes · cyan is the target · white is price · red is a warning**
+
+- **Gamma piles** hang BELOW the rail: Skylit's book via `cpRows` (same source as `regime2D`, so they can
+  never contradict the regime chip). Cut = **`CFG.nodeThresh`**, the existing ⚙ slider, default 20%.
+  Height = √magnitude. ⚠ nodeThresh is HAND-SET (⚖) — never measured.
+- **Skylit polarity**: purple = put-dominant = −gamma = ACCELERATOR; yellow = call-dominant = +gamma =
+  BRAKE. That forced the **target to CYAN `#4fd1e0`** and **STRETCHED to RED**.
+- **Three tiers**: money above · rail+ticks+dot on · piles below. They cannot collide by construction.
+
+### ⚠ THE DRIFTING-DOT FIX WAS INERT — SCHEMA STAMPS NOW
+v11.59 pinned the scale; a capture written BEFORE it had no `rr`, matched on date, and was reused, so the
+pin never fired (open 7695.86→7695.29 in minutes). **`EMOPEN_SCHEMA`** now versions the record and a
+stale/incomplete one is RE-TAKEN. **General rule: persisted state written by an older version can silently
+disable a newer guard. Every persisted store here should carry a stamp.**
+
+### 📦 THE RAW 60-STRIKE BOOK IS NOW RECORDED (`snap.book`)
+The feed sends **60** strikes (`nodes=60` — Skylit's `P20` control only changes THEIR canvas; no UI
+setting widens our feed). The export kept ~6, so **any threshold sweep measured our own filter, not the
+market.** `snap.book` = `[strike, callGEX $M, putGEX $M]` × 60. ⚠ **FORWARD-ONLY**, no back-fill.
+**This is what makes calibrating `nodeThresh` possible — weeks of it, then sweep.**
+
