+1. v11.59 `rr` drift (real, 0.05pt) · 2. v11.61 stale capture disabled that pin · 3. v11.63 the ANCHOR was
+recomputed from the SLIDING `closedCandles()` window (18pt) · 4. **v11.65 — v11.63's pin and v11.59's
+correction BOTH ran, so the anchor was scaled TWICE and drifted again** (7695.6 rendered 7709→7711).
+**ONE `useRr`, chosen once, applied once. No correction step exists any more.** The pre-scaling
+`open=openU*rr` line is deleted — it was the surface that allowed double-multiplication. A test counts the
+multiplications.
